<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Govindachandra (Chandra dynasty)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">11th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/govindachandra-of-the-gahadavala-dynasty">Govindachandra</a> was the last notable king of the Chandra dynasty of eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a> in the early 11th century. Inscriptions of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chola-empire">Chola</a> king Rajendra I record that his northern expedition of around 1021–1024 defeated Govindachandra of Vangala on its march to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ganges-plain">Ganges</a>. The Chandra line ended soon after, and the Varman dynasty succeeded in eastern Bengal.</p></div>
